The Home Assistant add-on packaging (config.yaml, Dockerfile, rootfs s6
services) follows the conventions used by diyhue/hassio-addon
(https://github.com/diyhue/hassio-addon), independently written for this
project. The `mac` add-on option follows the same documented rationale as
diyhue/hassio-addon's own `mac` option.

The v1 pairing endpoint's behaviour (no link-button timing gate; every
`POST /api` succeeds), the self-signed certificate's subject/validity/
extensions (CN=bridgeid, no SAN, fixed 2017-2038 validity window,
AuthorityKeyIdentifier), the TLS cipher/ALPN configuration, the SSDP
`SERVER` header format, the mDNS advertised port, the additional
`/api/{user}/config` fields (`analyticsconsent`, `portalconnection`,
`proxyaddress`, `proxyport`), and the v2 CLIP eventstream's `Last-Event-ID`
reconnect/replay support (hemera/hemera/objects/__init__.py,
hemera/hemera/api/v2/eventstream.py) follow the design used by Bifrost
(https://github.com/chrivers/bifrost, GPL-3.0, see its
src/routes/eventstream.rs) — independent reimplementations of the same
observed/documented behaviour, no source code copied.

